While perusing the monster attributes list the other day, I noticed two
unique monsters that don't seemed to be used in the game:

Charon, a 76th level peaceful monster
Ceberus, a 12th level dog in hell

Both are included in #ifdef CHARON statements, making it appear that CHARON
is some sort of unused option if the game.  I couldn't find any other use
of CHARON anywhere in the source.  Does anyone know what the plans are/were
for this stuff?  It seems like there are all sorts of interesting 
possibilities...a river Styx that you must pay Charon (through the nose) to 
cross...a "Gates of Hell" level beneath the castle, guarded by Cerberus...etc.

Just thought people might be interested, or know more about it....

